<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

  <title>Inside the Machine | Shelby Steward</title>

  <style>
    * {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    html {
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
    }

    body {
      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
      background: #080b12;
      color: #ffffff;
      line-height: 1.6;
      overflow-x: hidden;
    }

    a {
      color: inherit;
    }

    .container {
      width: min(1120px, 90%);
      margin: auto;
    }

    /* NAVIGATION */

    nav {
      position: fixed;
      top: 0;
      width: 100%;
      padding: 18px 0;
      z-index: 1000;
      background: rgba(8, 11, 18, 0.82);
      backdrop-filter: blur(15px);
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06);
    }

    .nav-inner {
      width: min(1120px, 90%);
      margin: auto;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .logo {
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: .07em;
    }

    .back-link {
      text-decoration: none;
      color: #5eead4;
      font-size: .9rem;
    }

    /* HERO */

    .hero {
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      position: relative;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 15% 20%, rgba(45,212,191,.13), transparent 30%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 85% 80%, rgba(59,130,246,.14), transparent 35%);
    }

    .hero-content {
      text-align: center;
      max-width: 950px;
      margin: auto;
      padding-top: 80px;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      color: #5eead4;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: .25em;
      font-size: .75rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
      line-height: .95;
      margin-bottom: 28px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, #ffffff, #99f6e4);
      -webkit-background-clip: text;
      -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    }

    .hero-sub {
      color: #a7b0c0;
      font-size: 1.15rem;
      max-width: 740px;
      margin: 0 auto 35px;
    }

    .hero-stats {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
      gap: 16px;
      margin: 45px auto;
    }

    .hero-stat {
      padding: 22px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1);
      border-radius: 16px;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,.035);
    }

    .hero-stat strong {
      display: block;
      font-size: 1.7rem;
      color: #5eead4;
    }

    .hero-stat span {
      color: #929caf;
      font-size: .8rem;
    }

    .start-button {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 15px 28px;
      background: #14b8a6;
      color: #031412;
      text-decoration: none;
      border-radius: 9px;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: .04em;
      transition: .25s ease;
    }

    .start-button:hover {
      transform: translateY(-3px);
      box-shadow: 0 15px 30px rgba(20,184,166,.25);
    }

    /* GENERIC SECTIONS */

    section {
      padding: 110px 0;
    }

    .section-number {
      font-size: .8rem;
      letter-spacing: .25em;
      color: #5eead4;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    .section-title {
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    .section-copy {
      color: #9da8bb;
      max-width: 760px;
      margin-bottom: 50px;
    }

    /* PIPELINE */

    .pipeline {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr);
      gap: 12px;
      margin-top: 40px;
    }

    .pipeline-stage {
      padding: 24px 14px;
      text-align: center;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);
      border-radius: 15px;
      background: #0e131e;
      transition: .3s ease;
    }

    .pipeline-stage:hover {
      border-color: #2dd4bf;
      transform: translateY(-7px);
    }

    .pipeline-stage span {
      display: block;
      color: #5eead4;
      font-size: .75rem;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    .pipeline-stage h3 {
      font-size: .95rem;
    }

    /* DATA SECTION */

    .scale-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
      gap: 20px;
    }

    .scale-card {
      padding: 30px;
      border-radius: 16px;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, #111827, #0b0f17);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);
    }

    .scale-card small {
      color: #8995a9;
    }

    .scale-card strong {
      display: block;
      font-size: 2.2rem;
      margin: 12px 0;
      color: #5eead4;
    }

    .scale-card p {
      color: #7f899c;
      font-size: .85rem;
    }

    /* COMPUTE */

    .compute-display {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 35px;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .mega-number {
      font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
      color: #5eead4;
      font-weight: 900;
      line-height: 1;
    }

    .mega-label {
      color: #8d98aa;
      margin-top: 10px;
    }

    .gpu-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(10, 1fr);
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .gpu {
      aspect-ratio: 1;
      background: #14b8a6;
      border-radius: 3px;
      opacity: .65;
      animation: pulse 2.4s infinite alternate;
    }

    @keyframes pulse {
      from {
        opacity: .3;
        transform: scale(.92);
      }

      to {
        opacity: .9;
        transform: scale(1);
      }
    }

    /* ENERGY */

    .energy-box {
      padding: 45px;
      background: #0c111b;
      border-radius: 20px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);
    }

    .energy-bar {
      height: 22px;
      background: #1c2431;
      border-radius: 20px;
      overflow: hidden;
      margin: 25px 0 15px;
    }

    .energy-fill {
      height: 100%;
      width: 0;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, #22c55e, #eab308, #ef4444);
      transition: width 2s ease;
    }

    .energy-box.visible .energy-fill {
      width: 92%;
    }

    .energy-stats {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 18px;
      margin-top: 30px;
    }

    .energy-stat {
      background: #111827;
      padding: 20px;
      border-radius: 13px;
    }

    .energy-stat strong {
      color: #5eead4;
      display: block;
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    /* COST TIMELINE */

    .cost-timeline {
      position: relative;
      margin-top: 60px;
    }

    .cost-item {
      padding: 30px;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
      border-left: 3px solid #14b8a6;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,.035);
      border-radius: 0 15px 15px 0;
    }

    .cost-item .year {
      color: #5eead4;
      font-weight: 800;
      font-size: .8rem;
    }

    .cost-item h3 {
      margin: 4px 0;
      font-size: 1.35rem;
    }

    .cost-item strong {
      font-size: 1.8rem;
    }

    /* MODEL TABLE */

    .model-table {
      overflow-x: auto;
    }

    table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      min-width: 800px;
    }

    th,
    td {
      padding: 18px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);
      text-align: left;
    }

    th {
      color: #5eead4;
      font-size: .78rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: .08em;
    }

    td {
      color: #b7c0cf;
    }

    /* TAKEAWAY */

    .takeaway {
      background:
        linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(20,184,166,.08), rgba(37,99,235,.08));
    }

    .takeaway-card {
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: auto;
      padding: 50px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(94,234,212,.2);
      border-radius: 22px;
      background: rgba(9,14,22,.8);
    }

    .takeaway-card h2 {
      font-size: 2.6rem;
      margin-bottom: 25px;
    }

    .takeaway-card p {
      color: #b0bacb;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    /* BUTTONS */

    .resource-links {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 15px;
      margin-top: 35px;
    }

    .secondary-button {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 13px 20px;
      border: 1px solid #2dd4bf;
      border-radius: 9px;
      color: #5eead4;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .secondary-button:hover {
      background: rgba(45,212,191,.08);
    }

    /* FOOTER */

    footer {
      padding: 45px 0;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);
      color: #7d8798;
      font-size: .85rem;
    }

    .footer-inner {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 20px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    /* REVEAL */

    .reveal {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(30px);
      transition: opacity .8s ease, transform .8s ease;
    }

    .reveal.visible {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }

    /* RESPONSIVE */

    @media(max-width: 900px) {
      .hero-stats,
      .scale-grid {
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      }

      .pipeline {
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      }

      .compute-display {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }

    @media(max-width: 600px) {
      section {
        padding: 75px 0;
      }

      .hero-stats,
      .scale-grid,
      .energy-stats {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .pipeline {
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      }

      .takeaway-card {
        padding: 30px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <nav>
    <div class="nav-inner">
      <div class="logo">SHELBY STEWARD</div>
      <a href="index.html" class="back-link">← Back to Portfolio</a>
    </div>
  </nav>


  <!-- HERO -->

  <header class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-content">

      <div class="eyebrow">Interactive AI Research Artifact</div>

      <h1>Inside the Machine</h1>

      <p class="hero-sub">
        What does it actually take to build generative AI?
        Follow a model from raw data to deployment and explore
        the resources hidden behind a single AI response.
      </p>

      <div class="hero-stats">

        <div class="hero-stat">
          <strong>13T+</strong>
          <span>Training Tokens</span>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-stat">
          <strong>25,000</strong>
          <span>GPUs</span>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-stat">
          <strong>~100</strong>
          <span>Training Days</span>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-stat">
          <strong>$100M+</strong>
          <span>Estimated Cost</span>
        </div>

      </div>

      <a href="#pipeline" class="start-button">
        START THE TRAINING RUN →
      </a>

    </div>
  </header>


  <!-- TRAINING PIPELINE -->

  <section id="pipeline">

    <div class="container reveal">

      <div class="section-number">01 / TRAIN THE MODEL</div>

      <h2 class="section-title">
        From Raw Data to Deployment
      </h2>

      <p class="section-copy">
        Generative AI does not emerge from one training step.
        It moves through a sequence of stages, each with its own
        technical requirements, costs, and opportunities for refinement.
      </p>

      <div class="pipeline">

        <div class="pipeline-stage">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Data Collection</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="pipeline-stage">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Preprocessing</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="pipeline-stage">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Pretraining</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="pipeline-stage">
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Fine-Tuning & RLHF</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="pipeline-stage">
          <span>05</span>
          <h3>Evaluation & Safety</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="pipeline-stage">
          <span>06</span>
          <h3>Deployment</h3>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- DATA -->

  <section>

    <div class="container reveal">

      <div class="section-number">02 / FEED IT</div>

      <h2 class="section-title">
        The Scale of Training Data
      </h2>

      <p class="section-copy">
        The volume of information used to train language models has increased
        dramatically. Larger datasets expand what models can learn, but data
        quality, diversity, licensing, and filtering remain just as important
        as raw scale.
      </p>

      <div class="scale-grid">

        <div class="scale-card">
          <small>GPT-3 · 2020</small>
          <strong>~300B</strong>
          <p>tokens</p>
        </div>

        <div class="scale-card">
          <small>LLaMA 2 · 2023</small>
          <strong>~2T</strong>
          <p>tokens</p>
        </div>

        <div class="scale-card">
          <small>GPT-4 · 2023</small>
          <strong>~13T</strong>
          <p>estimated tokens</p>
        </div>

        <div class="scale-card">
          <small>LLaMA 3.1 / 4</small>
          <strong>15T–30T+</strong>
          <p>tokens</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- COMPUTE -->

  <section>

    <div class="container reveal">

      <div class="section-number">03 / POWER IT</div>

      <h2 class="section-title">
        Compute at an Extraordinary Scale
      </h2>

      <div class="compute-display">

        <div>
          <div class="mega-number">2.1 × 10²⁵</div>
          <div class="mega-label">
            estimated FLOPs used to pretrain GPT-4
          </div>

          <p class="section-copy" style="margin-top:30px;">
            GPT-4 has been estimated to have trained on roughly
            25,000 NVIDIA A100 GPUs operating for approximately
            90 to 100 days.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="gpu-grid" id="gpuGrid"></div>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ENERGY -->

  <section>

    <div class="container">

      <div class="energy-box reveal">

        <div class="section-number">04 / POWER THE HARDWARE</div>

        <h2 class="section-title">
          AI Has a Physical Footprint
        </h2>

        <p class="section-copy">
          Training thousands of GPUs continuously for weeks or months
          requires data-center-scale electricity. Energy demand,
          emissions, infrastructure, and geographic power availability
          have become significant constraints in frontier AI development.
        </p>

        <div class="energy-bar">
          <div class="energy-fill"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="energy-stats">

          <div class="energy-stat">
            <strong>1.29 GWh</strong>
            <span>Estimated GPT-3 training energy</span>
          </div>

          <div class="energy-stat">
            <strong>552 t</strong>
            <span>Estimated GPT-3 CO₂ emissions</span>
          </div>

          <div class="energy-stat">
            <strong>~30 GWh</strong>
            <span>Estimated LLaMA 3.1 training energy</span>
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- COST -->

  <section>

    <div class="container reveal">

      <div class="section-number">05 / PAY FOR IT</div>

      <h2 class="section-title">
        The Cost of Frontier AI
      </h2>

      <p class="section-copy">
        As model scale increases, compute costs rise rapidly.
        Training frontier models has moved from millions of dollars
        into the tens or hundreds of millions.
      </p>

      <div class="cost-timeline">

        <div class="cost-item">
          <div class="year">2020</div>
          <h3>GPT-3</h3>
          <strong>$0.5M–$4.6M</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="cost-item">
          <div class="year">2023</div>
          <h3>GPT-4</h3>
          <strong>$78M–$100M+</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="cost-item">
          <div class="year">2023</div>
          <h3>Gemini Ultra</h3>
          <strong>~$191M</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="cost-item">
          <div class="year">FRONTIER SCALE</div>
          <h3>Next-Generation Models</h3>
          <strong>Approaching Billion-Dollar Training Runs</strong>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- MODEL COMPARISON -->

  <section>

    <div class="container reveal">

      <div class="section-number">06 / COMPARE</div>

      <h2 class="section-title">
        Four Models. Four Resource Profiles.
      </h2>

      <p class="section-copy">
        Public disclosure varies significantly across AI developers,
        making direct comparisons imperfect. Available estimates still
        reveal the rapid escalation of resource requirements.
      </p>

      <div class="model-table">

        <table>

          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Model</th>
              <th>Compute</th>
              <th>Estimated Cost</th>
              <th>Energy / Emissions</th>
              <th>Data Scale</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>

          <tbody>

            <tr>
              <td>GPT-3</td>
              <td>~3.1 × 10²³ FLOPs</td>
              <td>$0.5M–$4.6M</td>
              <td>1.29 GWh / 552 t CO₂</td>
              <td>~300B tokens</td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>LLaMA 2 70B</td>
              <td>~1.7M GPU-hours</td>
              <td>Not disclosed</td>
              <td>539 t CO₂</td>
              <td>~2T tokens</td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>GPT-4</td>
              <td>~2.1 × 10²⁵ FLOPs</td>
              <td>$78M–$100M+</td>
              <td>Not disclosed</td>
              <td>~13T tokens</td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>LLaMA 4 Scout + Maverick</td>
              <td>7.38M GPU-hours</td>
              <td>Not disclosed</td>
              <td>5.17 GWh</td>
              <td>~30T+ tokens</td>
            </tr>

          </tbody>

        </table>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- TAKEAWAY -->

  <section class="takeaway">

    <div class="container">

      <div class="takeaway-card reveal">

        <div class="section-number">07 / MY TAKEAWAY</div>

        <h2>
          AI Isn't Intangible.
        </h2>

        <p>
          When we interact with a generative AI model, it can feel almost
          weightless: a prompt goes in, and an answer appears seconds later.
          Studying the training process changed that perspective for me.
        </p>

        <p>
          Behind that response is an enormous physical and financial
          infrastructure involving data, GPUs, electricity, human feedback,
          engineering time, and millions of dollars.
        </p>

        <p>
          What stood out to me most was not simply how expensive AI is to build,
          but how interconnected every resource is. More data requires more
          compute. More compute requires more energy. More energy and hardware
          increase cost.
        </p>

        <p>
          None of those resources guarantee a better model unless the data,
          training strategy, evaluation, and alignment are effective.
          Understanding those tradeoffs gave me a very different appreciation
          for what actually happens before a model ever receives its first
          user prompt.
        </p>

        <div class="resource-links">

          <a href="inside-the-machine-research.pptx"
             class="secondary-button"
             target="_blank">
            View Original Research Presentation
          </a>

          <a href="index.html"
             class="secondary-button">
            Return to Portfolio
          </a>

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <footer>

    <div class="container footer-inner">

      <div>
        © 2026 Shelby Steward
      </div>

      <div>
        M.S. Artificial Intelligence – Data Analytics
      </div>

    </div>

  </footer>


  <script>

    // Build GPU visualization

    const gpuGrid = document.getElementById("gpuGrid");

    for (let i = 0; i < 100; i++) {

      const gpu = document.createElement("div");

      gpu.classList.add("gpu");

      gpu.style.animationDelay =
        `${Math.random() * 2}s`;

      gpuGrid.appendChild(gpu);
    }


    // Scroll reveal animation

    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
      entries => {

        entries.forEach(entry => {

          if (entry.isIntersecting) {
            entry.target.classList.add("visible");
          }

        });

      },
      {
        threshold: 0.15
      }
    );


    document
      .querySelectorAll(".reveal")
      .forEach(element => observer.observe(element));

  </script>

</body>
